<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23328" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infundĭbŭlum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infūd-,
			infīd-</span></b> ), i, n.
		infundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a funnel</i> (cf. infurnibulum). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 18,
				6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 10, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">11, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Pall. 7, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10,
				10, 12</span></i> and 13 (infidibula). — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>the
				funnel</i> in a mill, through which the grain is poured, <i>the hopper</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10,
			10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
